{
 "cells": [
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "# Real-Time Multi-Frame VSR Training\n",
    "This notebook covers downloading the dataset via Kaggle, preprocessing it on Colab, training the network, and exporting the ONNX model."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 1. Setup & Mount Google Drive\n",
    "We mount Google Drive to save our trained model checkpoints so they aren't lost if Colab disconnects."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from google.colab import drive\n",
    "drive.mount('/content/drive')\n",
    "\n",
    "!mkdir -p /content/drive/MyDrive/VSR_Checkpoints"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 2. Clone Repository & Install Requirements"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "# NOTE: If you are actively developing, you can upload your project zip or clone your GitHub repo here.\n",
    "# For now, we assume the code is uploaded or cloned into /content/vsr-project\n",
    "!git clone https://github.com/your-username/vsr-project.git\n",
    "%cd vsr-project\n",
    "!pip install -r requirements.txt"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 3. Kaggle Setup & Dataset Download\n",
    "Upload your `kaggle.json` file when prompted. Replace `<USERNAME/DATASET>` with the actual Kaggle dataset slug."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "from google.colab import files\n",
    "import os\n",
    "\n",
    "# Upload kaggle.json\n",
    "uploaded = files.upload()\n",
    "\n",
    "# Setup Kaggle API\n",
    "!mkdir -p ~/.kaggle\n",
    "!cp kaggle.json ~/.kaggle/\n",
    "!chmod 600 ~/.kaggle/kaggle.json\n",
    "\n",
    "# REPLACE this with the actual Kaggle slug for the 9.26GB dataset you found!\n",
    "kaggle_slug = \"username/dataset-name\"\n",
    "\n",
    "!kaggle datasets download -d $kaggle_slug\n",
    "!echo \"Unzipping dataset...\"\n",
    "!unzip -q *.zip -d /content/vimeo_septuplet"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 4. Preprocess Dataset\n",
    "Apply synthetic degradations (blur, noise, etc.) and pre-compute optical flow. We save this to the local Colab disk (fast) rather than Google Drive (slow IO)."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "!python src/vsr/dataset.py --vimeo /content/vimeo_septuplet --out /content/processed_dataset --split train --frames 7"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 5. Stage A: Single-Frame Pretraining\n",
    "Train the network to act as a standard single-image upscaler first. Checkpoints go directly to your Google Drive."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "!python src/vsr/train.py --data /content/processed_dataset --out /content/drive/MyDrive/VSR_Checkpoints --stage A"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 6. Stage B: Recurrent Finetuning\n",
    "Train the network using Truncated Backpropagation Through Time (T-BPTT) on the 7-frame sequences."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "!python src/vsr/train.py --data /content/processed_dataset --out /content/drive/MyDrive/VSR_Checkpoints --stage B"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "### 7. Export to ONNX\n",
    "Export the fully trained model to ONNX so it can be downloaded and run on your local laptop's CPU."
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "code",
   "execution_count": null,
   "metadata": {},
   "outputs": [],
   "source": [
    "!python src/vsr/export_onnx.py --checkpoint /content/drive/MyDrive/VSR_Checkpoints/model_stage_B_epoch_100.pth --out /content/drive/MyDrive/VSR_Checkpoints/vsr_model.onnx\n",
    "\n",
    "print(\"Training and export complete! You can now download vsr_model.onnx from your Google Drive.\")"
   ]
  }
